<%= lato_page_head "Documentation" %>

<h2>How to use Lato Spaces</h2>

<p>
  <code>lato_spaces</code> adds workspaces or groups to a Lato application.
  Use it when users must work inside one selected group and application data must be separated by group.
</p>

<h3>Installation</h3>

<p>Requires Rails 8.1.3.1 or newer in the 8.1 series and Lato 3.25.0 or newer.
Existing applications must run <code>rails lato:install:migrations</code> and <code>rails db:migrate</code>
before deployment. Previous sessions are invalidated.</p>

<p>Add Lato Spaces to the application Gemfile:</p>

<pre><code>gem "lato"
gem "lato_spaces"</code></pre>

<p>Install the engine and run migrations:</p>

<pre><code>bundle
rails lato_spaces:install:application
rails lato_spaces:install:migrations
rails db:migrate</code></pre>

<p>Mount the engine in <code>config/routes.rb</code>:</p>

<pre><code>Rails.application.routes.draw do
  mount LatoSpaces::Engine =&gt; "/lato-spaces"

  # ...
end</code></pre>

<p>Import styles in <code>app/assets/stylesheets/application.scss</code>:</p>

<pre><code>@import "lato_spaces/application";</code></pre>

<p>Import JavaScript in <code>app/javascript/application.js</code>:</p>

<pre><code>import "lato_spaces/application"</code></pre>

<p>Add a menu entry to the group selection page, for example in <code>app/views/layouts/lato/_navbar-nav_content.html.erb</code>:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;%= lato_navbar_nav_item :lato_spaces, lato_spaces.root_path do %&gt;
  Spaces
&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>

<p>
  Upgrading from 3.2.0 or earlier: run <code>rails lato_spaces:install:migrations</code> and <code>rails db:migrate</code>.
  The new migration removes duplicate memberships and associations, then adds unique indexes.
</p>

<h3>Configuration</h3>

<p>Configure group behavior in an initializer:</p>

<pre><code>LatoSpaces.configure do |config|
  config.setgroup_redirect_path = :dashboard_path
  config.setgroup_auto_after_login = false
  config.setgroup_auto_after_login_if_single = true
  config.permit_group_creation = false
  config.permit_group_management = false
  config.permit_group_preferred = false
end</code></pre>

<div class="table-responsive">
  <table class="table table-striped align-middle">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Option</th>
        <th scope="col">Default</th>
        <th scope="col">Use for</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>setgroup_redirect_path</code></td>
        <td><code>nil</code></td>
        <td>Name of a host application route helper without arguments (e.g. <code>:dashboard_path</code>). Users are redirected there after selecting a group. With <code>nil</code> they return to the Spaces page.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>setgroup_auto_after_login</code></td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td>Select a group automatically when the user opens the Spaces page without a selected group: the preferred group first, otherwise the first by name. Requires <code>setgroup_redirect_path</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>setgroup_auto_after_login_if_single</code></td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td>Same as above, only when the user belongs to exactly one group. Requires <code>setgroup_redirect_path</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>group_icon</code></td>
        <td><code>"bi bi-people-fill"</code></td>
        <td>Bootstrap Icons class shown on group cards.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>group_params</code></td>
        <td><code>%i[name]</code></td>
        <td>Permitted group form params.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>membership_params</code></td>
        <td><code>%i[email]</code></td>
        <td>Permitted membership form params.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>permit_group_creation</code></td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td>Allow non-admin users to create groups. The creator becomes the first member.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>permit_group_management</code></td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td>Allow non-admin members to manage their own groups (see permissions below).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>permit_group_preferred</code></td>
        <td><code>false</code></td>
        <td>Allow users to mark a preferred group. It is listed first and used by automatic selection.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p>
  Automatic selection runs only when the user visits the Spaces page (<code>lato_spaces.root_path</code>),
  so make the post-login flow land there.
  Never permit <code>lato_user_id</code>, <code>lato_invitation_id</code> or <code>lato_spaces_group_id</code>
  in <code>group_params</code> or <code>membership_params</code>.
</p>

<h3>Permissions</h3>

<p>
  Users must be logged into Lato. Users with <code>lato_spaces_admin</code> can select and manage all groups.
  Other users can only select groups where they are current members.
  Protected requests recheck membership and clear the selected group if access was revoked.
</p>

<pre><code>user = Lato::User.find_by(email: "admin@example.com")
user.update!(lato_spaces_admin: true)</code></pre>

<div class="table-responsive">
  <table class="table table-striped align-middle">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Action</th>
        <th scope="col">Admin</th>
        <th scope="col">Member with <code>permit_group_management</code></th>
        <th scope="col">Member</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Select a group</th><td>Any group, also from the group page</td><td>Own groups</td><td>Own groups</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">List all groups</th><td>Yes</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Create groups</th><td>Yes</td><td>With <code>permit_group_creation</code></td><td>With <code>permit_group_creation</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Rename or delete a group</th><td>Any group</td><td>Own groups</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Add registered users</th><td>Any group</td><td>Own groups</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Invite unregistered emails</th><td>Any group</td><td>Own groups, only if Lato signup is enabled</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Remove members, resend invitations</th><td>Any group</td><td>Own groups, except the last registered member</td><td>No</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p>
  Groups have no roles yet: with <code>permit_group_management</code> every member has the same powers,
  including deleting the group and its data. Enable it only for trusted members.
  Adding members and resending invitations are rate limited.
</p>

<h3>Invitations</h3>

<ul>
  <li>The email is normalized (stripped and downcased).</li>
  <li>A registered user is added immediately. Non-admins see members by email; full names are shown to admins only.</li>
  <li>An existing pending Lato invitation is reused; otherwise a new invitation is created and emailed.</li>
  <li>When the invitation is accepted, the membership moves to the new user.</li>
  <li>A user or invitation can belong to a group only once.</li>
  <li>Lato invitations bypass <code>auth_disable_signup</code>: when signup is disabled only admins can invite unregistered emails.</li>
</ul>

<h3>What users can do</h3>

<ul>
  <li>See available groups.</li>
  <li>Select the active group for the current session.</li>
  <li>Work only with data that belongs to the selected group.</li>
  <li>Add or invite users to a group when management is allowed.</li>
  <li>Choose a preferred group when enabled.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Protecting application pages</h3>

<p>
  Include the group helper in controllers that require a selected group,
  then require both Lato authentication and group selection.
</p>

<pre><code>class ApplicationController &lt; Lato::ApplicationController
  include LatoSpaces::Groupable
end

class ProjectsController &lt; ApplicationController
  before_action :authenticate_session
  before_action :authenticate_group

  def index
    @projects = Project.for_lato_spaces_group(@session.get(:spaces_group_id))
  end
end</code></pre>

<p><code>LatoSpaces::Groupable</code> adds these protected methods:</p>

<ul>
  <li><code>authenticate_group</code>: checks that the selected group is still accessible. Otherwise it clears the selection and redirects to the Spaces page (HTML) or responds <code>403 Forbidden</code> (JSON).</li>
  <li><code>session_group_create(group_id)</code>: selects a group the user can access, returns <code>false</code> otherwise.</li>
  <li><code>session_group_destroy</code>: clears the selected group.</li>
</ul>

<p>Read <code>@session.get(:spaces_group_id)</code> only in controllers protected by <code>authenticate_group</code>.</p>

<h3>Associating application data with groups</h3>

<p>
  Add Lato Spaces associations to application records that must belong to one or more groups.
</p>

<pre><code>class Project &lt; ApplicationRecord
  include LatoSpaces::Associable
end</code></pre>

<ul>
  <li><code>for_lato_spaces_group(group_id)</code>: records of a group (<code>nil</code> returns nothing; with an array of ids add <code>.distinct</code> to avoid duplicates).</li>
  <li><code>with_lato_spaces_groups</code> / <code>without_lato_spaces_groups</code>: records with or without groups.</li>
  <li><code>lato_spaces_group</code>, <code>lato_spaces_group_id</code>: first group of the record.</li>
  <li><code>add_to_lato_spaces_group(id)</code>, <code>remove_from_lato_spaces_group(id)</code>, <code>switch_lato_spaces_group(id)</code>: return <code>true</code> or <code>false</code> and add errors to the record on failure.</li>
</ul>

<p>When records must always belong to exactly one group, add the stricter concerns after <code>LatoSpaces::Associable</code>:</p>

<pre><code>class Project &lt; ApplicationRecord
  include LatoSpaces::Associable
  include LatoSpaces::AssociableRequired
  include LatoSpaces::AssociableUnique
end</code></pre>

<ul>
  <li><code>AssociableRequired</code>: an existing <code>lato_spaces_group_id</code> is required on create. <strong>Destroying the association destroys the record</strong>: removing it from its group or deleting the group deletes it.</li>
  <li><code>AssociableUnique</code>: a record can belong to one group only.</li>
  <li>Both only affect the models that include them.</li>
</ul>

<p>Create records with the current selected group, never with a group id from request params:</p>

<pre><code>Project.create!(
  name: "Project 1",
  lato_spaces_group_id: @session.get(:spaces_group_id)
)</code></pre>

<p>Deleting a group removes its memberships and associations, and destroys every <code>AssociableRequired</code> record of the group.</p>

<h3>Customizing group forms</h3>

<p>
  <code>rails lato_spaces:install:application</code> copies overridable partials into
  <code>app/views/layouts/lato_spaces/</code> (<code>_group-form-extra_content</code>, <code>_membership-form-extra_content</code>,
  <code>_group-informations_content</code>) and the <code>LatoSpacesMembershipApplication</code> model concern.
  Edit them to add custom fields or extra information to group and membership pages.
  Custom fields must also be permitted with <code>group_params</code> or <code>membership_params</code>.
</p>
